Stop [E0128]: Zip inputs have different lengths under `strict` policy
  --> zip_strict_mismatch.jet:2 in run
    |
2 |     print([1, 2, 3].zip([10, 20]).to_list().len())
    |     ^^^^^
 Why: Strict `zip` requires every input to end on the same row.
 Fix: Use `zip_short` to intentionally truncate or `zip_pad` to intentionally pad; neither changes strictness automatically.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0128
